.TH NAP 1 "2025" "ChonkOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nap \- power and lid management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nap
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nap
reports power state and controls systemd-inhibit locks and the lid switch
action. Exit status is 0 on success and 1 on any error; \fBnap stay\fR
returns the wrapped command's exit code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a table.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Report batteries (status, percent, health percent, watts), AC adapters,
thermal zones, and the configured lid action from
.IR /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/90-chonkos-lid.conf .
.TP
.BR stay " " DURATION
Hold a systemd-inhibit lock (idle:sleep:handle-lid-switch, mode block) for
DURATION, e.g. 90s, 45m, 1h30m. DURATION must be positive.
.TP
.BR stay " \-\- " COMMAND " [ARG...]"
Hold the inhibitor lock until COMMAND exits; the exit code of nap is the
exit code of COMMAND (128+signal if killed). With \fB\-\-json\fR the child's
stdout is redirected to stderr and nap prints {"exit_code": N}.
.TP
.BR lid " status"
Print the current lid drop-in contents.
.TP
.BR lid " sleep"
Set HandleLidSwitch and HandleLidSwitchExternalPower to suspend. Requires
root. Never restarts systemd-logind; only runs
.BR "systemctl reload systemd-logind" .
.TP
.BR lid " ignore"
Set both lid actions to ignore. Requires root; same reload behavior.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
nap status
.TP
nap --json status
.TP
nap stay 1h30m
.TP
nap stay -- make -j4
.TP
nap lid status
.TP
sudo nap lid ignore
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/90-chonkos-lid.conf
ChonkOS logind lid drop-in written by \fBnap lid\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chonk (1),
.BR whisker (1)
